#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:572
msgid ""
"Move your newly created ``svg`` icons (optimized or not) into that folder."
msgstr "새로 생성된 ``svg`` 아이콘(최적화 여부)을 해당 폴더로 이동합니다."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:574
msgid ""
"Recompile the engine and run the editor. Now the icon(s) will appear in "
"editor's interface where appropriate."
msgstr ""
"엔진을 다시 컴파일하고 편집기를 실행합니다. 이제 해당 아이콘이 편집기 인터페"
"이스에 나타납니다."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:577
msgid ""
"If you'd like to store your icons somewhere else within your module, add the "
"following code snippet to ``config.py`` to override the default path:"
msgstr ""
"모듈 내 다른 곳에 아이콘을 저장하려면 다음 코드 조각을 ``config.py``에 추가하"
"여 기본 경로를 재정의하세요."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:586
msgid "Summing up"
msgstr "요약"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:588
msgid "Remember to:"
msgstr "다음을 기억하세요:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:590
msgid "Use ``GDCLASS`` macro for inheritance, so Godot can wrap it."
msgstr ""
"상속을 위해 ``GDCLASS`` 매크로를 사용하면 Godot가 이를 래핑할 수 있습니다."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:591
msgid ""
"Use ``_bind_methods`` to bind your functions to scripting, and to allow them "
"to work as callbacks for signals."
msgstr ""
"``_bind_methods``를 사용하여 함수를 스크립팅에 바인딩하고 함수가 시그널에 대"
"한 콜백으로 작동하도록 허용합니다."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:593
msgid ""
"**Avoid multiple inheritance for classes exposed to Godot**, as ``GDCLASS`` "
"doesn't support this. You can still use multiple inheritance in your own "
"classes as long as they're not exposed to Godot's scripting API."
msgstr ""
"**Godot에 노출된 클래스에 대한 다중 상속을 피하세요**, ``GDCLASS``는 이를 지"
"원하지 않습니다. Godot의 스크립팅 API에 노출되지 않는 한 자신의 클래스에서 다"
"중 상속을 계속 사용할 수 있습니다."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:597
msgid ""
"But this is not all, depending what you do, you will be greeted with some "
"(hopefully positive) surprises."
msgstr ""
"그러나 이것이 전부는 아닙니다. 무엇을 하느냐에 따라 (희망적으로 긍정적인) 놀"
"라움을 맞이하게 될 것입니다."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:600
msgid ""
"If you inherit from :ref:`class_Node` (or any derived node type, such as "
"Sprite2D), your new class will appear in the editor, in the inheritance tree "
"in the \"Add Node\" dialog."
msgstr ""
":ref:`class_Node`(또는 Sprite2D와 같은 파생된 노드 유형)에서 상속하는 경우 "
"새 클래스가 편집기의 \"노드 추가\" 대화 상자에 있는 상속 트리에 나타납니다."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:603
msgid ""
"If you inherit from :ref:`class_Resource`, it will appear in the resource "
"list, and all the exposed properties can be serialized when saved/loaded."
msgstr ""
":ref:`class_Resource`에서 상속하면 리소스 목록에 나타나며 노출된 모든 속성은 "
"저장/로드 시 직렬화될 수 있습니다."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:606
msgid ""
"By this same logic, you can extend the Editor and almost any area of the "
"engine."
msgstr ""
"이와 동일한 논리로 편집기와 엔진의 거의 모든 영역을 확장할 수 있습니다."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/vendor_runtime_module.rst:4
msgid "Vendor Runtime Module"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/vendor_runtime_module.rst:6
msgid ""
"A Vendor Runtime Module is a :ref:`Godot module <doc_custom_modules_in_cpp>` "
"which is only applicable at runtime in a running project. It is created like "
"a regular :ref:`custom C++ module <doc_custom_modules_in_cpp>`, but is "
"packaged using an :ref:`editor plugin <doc_making_plugins>` to make the "
"functionality it provides easily accessible and usable within a *stock* "
"Godot project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/vendor_runtime_module.rst:15
msgid ""
"Vendor runtime modules provide developers with access to vendor-specific "
"optimizations, features, and/or platforms for their running projects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/vendor_runtime_module.rst:18
msgid ""
"This provides benefits to vendors who are able to expose their technologies "
"to all developers, and improve and refine them in a rapid, iterative, and "
"frictionless manner. This also provides benefits to developers and users who "
"are able to access and use a diverse range of vendor technologies to improve "
"their games."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/vendor_runtime_module.rst:24
#, fuzzy
